      "end_s": 167.7,
      "duration_s": 22.47,
      "visual_objective": "",
      "narration": "Let me draw where one hundred dollars at the register goes. About eighty-nine dollars pays the supplier for the goods. About eleven dollars is left. Most of that pays for the stores and the staff. What remains is a tiny sliver of profit. Hold on to that picture, because the real profit is coming from somewhere else.",
