    {
      "index": 28,
      "id": "s27_balance",
      "segment": "m4_balance",
      "type": "engine_cartoon",
      "start_s": 464.17,
      "end_s": 484.4,
      "duration_s": 20.23,
      "visual_objective": "",
      "narration": "Look at the balance sheet. At the end of August twenty twenty-six, Costco held about nineteen point three billion dollars of goods in its warehouses. At the same moment, it owed its suppliers twenty-two point six billion dollars. It owed more than the value of everything on its shelves.",
      "keyframes": [
        {
          "param": "items[0].bars[1].at.cue",
          "cue": "it owed its suppliers",
          "label": "items[0].bars[1].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 12.43,
          "absolute_s": 476.59
        },
        {
          "param": "items[1].at.cue",
          "cue": "It owed more than",
          "label": "items[1].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 16.55,
          "absolute_s": 480.72
        }
      ],
      "unresolved_cues": [],
      "assets": [
        "font:inter"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "tenk"
      ],
      "transition_out": "scan"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "id": "s28_turns",
      "segment": "m4_turns",
      "type": "engine_cartoon",
      "start_s": 484.4,
      "end_s": 512.23,
      "duration_s": 27.83,
      "visual_objective": "",
      "narration": "How is that possible? Speed. By our calculation, Costco's entire inventory sells through about fourteen times a year. A typical item sits in the warehouse for less than a month. If the supplier gives Costco about a month to pay, the cash from the customer often arrives first. A slower store, where goods sit on the shelf for months, would have to find that money somewhere else.",
      "keyframes": [
        {
          "param": "items[1].at.cue",
          "cue": "By our calculation",
          "label": "items[1].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 2.88,
          "absolute_s": 487.28
        },
        {
          "param": "items[0].goneAt.cue",
          "cue": "sells through",
          "label": "items[0].goneAt.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 7.21,
          "absolute_s": 491.61
        },
        {
          "param": "items[1].steps[1][0].cue",
          "cue": "fourteen times",
          "label": "items[1].steps[1][0].cue",
          "scene_time_s": 8.37,
          "absolute_s": 492.77
        },
        {
          "param": "items[2].at.cue",
          "cue": "A typical item sits",
          "label": "items[2].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 10.82,
          "absolute_s": 495.22
        },
        {
          "param": "items[3].at.cue",
          "cue": "often arrives first",
          "label": "items[3].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 19.52,
          "absolute_s": 503.92
        },
        {
          "param": "cam[1].at.cue",
          "cue": "A slower store",
          "label": "cam[1].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 21.66,
          "absolute_s": 506.06
        }
      ],
      "unresolved_cues": [],
      "assets": [
        "font:inter"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "tenk"
      ],
      "transition_out": "scan"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "id": "p29_cycle",
      "segment": "m4_draw",
      "type": "engine_draw",
      "start_s": 512.23,
      "end_s": 534.87,
      "duration_s": 22.63,
      "visual_objective": "",
      "narration": "Let me draw the cash cycle. Day zero, a pallet arrives. A few weeks later, members have bought it, and the cash is in Costco's bank. Only later does the bill to the supplier come due. In between, Costco holds billions of dollars that are really its suppliers' money, and it can use that money to run the business.",
      "keyframes": [
        {
          "param": "strokes[0].start.cue",
          "cue": "Let me draw the cash cycle",
          "label": "strokes[0].start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 0.35,
          "absolute_s": 512.58
        },
        {
          "param": "draw_start.cue",
          "cue": "Day zero",
          "label": "draw_start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 2.69,
          "absolute_s": 514.92
        },
        {
          "param": "strokes[1].start.cue",
          "cue": "Day zero",
          "label": "strokes[1].start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 2.69,
          "absolute_s": 514.92
        },
        {
          "param": "strokes[2].start.cue",
          "cue": "members have bought it",
          "label": "strokes[2].start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 6.62,
          "absolute_s": 518.85
        },
        {
          "param": "strokes[3].start.cue",
          "cue": "Only later does the bill",
          "label": "strokes[3].start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 10.41,
          "absolute_s": 522.64
        },
        {
          "param": "strokes[4].start.cue",
          "cue": "In between",
          "label": "strokes[4].start.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 13.86,
          "absolute_s": 526.09
        },
        {
          "param": "actions[0].at.cue",
          "cue": "In between",
          "label": "actions[0].at.cue",
          "scene_time_s": 14.16,
          "absolute_s": 526.39
        }
      ],
      "unresolved_cues": [],
      "assets": [
        "font:inter"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "tenk"
      ],
      "transition_out": "scan"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "id": "s30_t4",
      "segment": "m4_transition",
      "type": "kinetic_text",
      "start_s": 534.87,
      "end_s": 541.4,
      "duration_s": 6.53,
      "visual_objective": "Kinetic typography: lines enter word by word on narration cues",
      "narration": "One more piece ties everything together. The members who spend the most.",
      "keyframes": [
        {
          "param": "lines[0].cue",
          "cue": "One more piece",
          "label": "One more piece…",
          "scene_time_s": 0.35,
