      "visual_objective": "",
      "narration": "So how does Costco make money selling things cheap? It does not really try to profit on the goods. It sells access. The cheap prices are the product that keeps millions of people paying, every single year, for the privilege of shopping there. The store is the bait. The membership is the business. And for members, the deal works only as long as the savings are bigger than the fee. That is the promise Costco has to keep, every single year, to stay on top.",
